# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the TSan build (docs/sanitizers.md).
#
# Third-party code only. vcpkg dependencies are prebuilt without TSan instrumentation, so TSan
# cannot see their atomics, memory barriers or internal locks; vendored submodules are not
# patched here. A report with a frame in src/, apps/ or tests/ that is not explained by one of
# the entries below is a bug to fix, never an entry to add. Patterns name third-party
# functions: TSan suppresses a report when any frame of either access matches.

# glibc: spatialite_init_ex() (libspatialite, run by Database::afterOpen for every connection)
# calls setlocale(LC_NUMERIC, "POSIX"). glibc serialises setlocale() calls with its internal
# __libc_setlocale_lock, which TSan cannot see, so two connections opening at once look like a
# race on the LC_ALL name string (setname/new_composite_name).
race:setlocale

# SQLite: the WAL-index header is read without a lock by design; walIndexTryHdr() reads two
# copies separated by memory barriers and retries when they differ (sqlite3.c, "WAL-index
# header"). The barriers are in uninstrumented code.
race:walIndexTryHdr
race:walIndexWriteHdr

# libcurl via PDAL: PDAL's Connector (io/private/connector/Connector.cpp, used by readers.copc)
# builds a User-Agent with curl_version() for every reader, and curl_version() rewrites a
# static buffer (lib/version.c) with the same bytes on each call. Concurrent tile renders open
# concurrent COPC readers.
race:curl_version

# cctz: TimeZoneMutex() is a function-local static (time_zone_impl.cc); its thread-safe
# initialisation guard runs in uninstrumented code, so the first lock after another thread
# created the mutex looks unsynchronised.
race:TimeZoneMutex

# GDAL: a lock-order inversion between two mutexes that are both locked from uninstrumented
# GDAL code on a GDAL worker thread (created by CPLCreateJoinableThread), one of them through
# the job-queue condition variable in CPLWorkerThreadPool::GetNextJob
# (port/cpl_worker_thread_pool.cpp). No DroneDB frame is in any of its stacks.
deadlock:CPLWorkerThreadPool
